title: 'statement-store: announce hashes ahead of bodies in the initial sync'
doc:
- audience: [Node Operator, Node Dev]
  description: |-
    A node with `--statement-dht` now syncs a full `statement/4` peer in two steps. It announces
    the short hashes of the statements that it holds for the peer, the peer answers which of them
    it lacks, and only those bodies go out. A peer that reconnects, repeats its filter after
    major sync, or changes its filter no longer downloads statements that it already holds.
    Light peers and peers below `statement/4` get bodies as before.
    The `StatementStore` trait has two new required methods, `hashes_by_topic` and
    `knows_short_hash`.
    New counters: `substrate_sync_statement_announced_hashes_sent_total`,
    `substrate_sync_statement_announced_hashes_requested_total`,
    `substrate_sync_statement_announced_hashes_received_total` and
    `substrate_sync_statement_announced_hashes_wanted_total`. The histogram
    `substrate_sync_initial_sync_duration_seconds` has a new outcome `unanswered`.
crates:
- name: sp-statement-store
  bump: major
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: minor
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: minor
